===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:open}}
Adjective from {{inh|en|enm|open}}, from {{inh|en|ang|open|t=open}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*opan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*upanaz|t=open}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*upo|t=up from under, over}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
* {{cog|sco|apen|t=open}}
* {{cog|stq|eepen|t=open}}
* {{cog|fy|iepen|t=open}}
* {{cog|cim|offe|t=open}}
* {{cog|nl|open|t=open}}
* {{cog|de|offen|t=open}}
* {{cog|wym|ufa}}, {{m|wym|uffa|t=open}}
* {{cog|yi|אָפֿן|t=open}}
* {{cog|da|åben|t=open}}
* {{cog|is|opinn|t=open}}
* {{cog|nb|åpen|t=open}}
* {{cog|nn|open|t=open}}
* {{cog|sv|öppen|t=open}}
Compare also {{cog|la|supinus|t=on one's back, supine}}, {{cog|sq|hap|t=to open}}. Related to {{m|en|up}}.
{{col-bottom}}

Verb from {{inh|en|enm|openen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|openian|t=to open}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*opanōn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*upanōną|t=to raise; lift; open}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*upanaz|t=open|pos=adjective}}. Cognate with {{cog|stq|eepenje|t=to open}}, {{cog|fy|iepenje|t=to open}}, {{cog|nl|openen|t=to open}}, {{cog|de|öffnen|t=to open}}, {{cog|da|åbne|t=to open}}, {{cog|sv|öppna|t=to open}}, {{cog|nb|åpne|t=to open}}, {{cog|nn|-}} and {{cog|is|opna|t=to open}}. Related to {{cog|en|up}}.

Noun from {{inh|en|enm|open|t=an aperture or opening}}, from the verb. In the sports sense, however, a shortening of “open competition”.

